    "_id": "6tN3rTrPlqYk9mvX",
    "flags": {
        "cinderfall": {
            "tagline": "Everything here is still trying to grow. That's the problem, and it's also the only tool you've got.",
            "role": "Terrain-warper — the map is the weapon",
            "pillar": "Nature — the first Primal caster",
            "hpFormula": "8 + Con / level",
            "keyAbilityText": "Wisdom",
            "spellcastingText": "Primal, prepared (Wisdom)",
            "spellcastingTradition": "Primal",
            "spellcastingPreparation": "prepared",
            "terms": [
                [
                    "Bloomrot",
                    "<strong>Your class resource — and it is never spent.</strong> A single needle on a two-sided track running from Grey through zero to Green. Every spell you cast pushes it one step one way or the other. Where it sits decides what you can cast next (§3)."
                ],
                [
                    "Green",
                    "<strong>Growth that doesn't ask permission.</strong> Root through a wall, choke a road, bloom a corpse into a thicket. Not \"good\" — just alive, and indifferent to what was there first."
                ],
                [
                    "Grey",
                    "<strong>Decay put to work.</strong> Soften steel, rot a rope, hollow a thing out from the inside. Not \"evil\" — the Wastes run on rot as much as on growth, and a Warden who refuses to touch it is half a use to anyone."
                ],
                [
                    "Bloom tag",
                    "<strong>Which way a spell pushes the needle</strong> — every Seed-Warden spell is tagged Green, Grey, or <em>either</em> (you choose as you cast). Printed on every entry in <a href=\"spells-abilities.html\" style=\"color:var(--accent);\">What You Learned</a>."
                ],
                [
                    "Charge requirement",
                    "<strong>The gate on your deeper spells.</strong> \"Requires Green 2\" means the needle must already sit at Green 2 or further out before you cast. Commit to a side and it opens up; sit at zero and the whole back half of your list is closed."
                ],
                [
                    "Cutting",
                    "<strong>Your subclass</strong> — Greenline, Blightline, or Turnwise (§2). Chosen at 1st level. It doesn't restrict which spells you can learn; it changes what the needle <em>does for you</em> when it's sitting where your Cutting likes it."
                ],
                [
                    "Blight-Shape",
                    "<strong>Your form-change, replacing wild shape</strong> — a mutant template rather than an animal (§4). Which loadout you get depends on which side of the needle is live at that instant, and it re-evaluates mid-fight."
                ],
                [
                    "[TERRAIN]",
                    "<strong>The tag that makes this class what it is.</strong> A spell marked TERRAIN has no duration. It changes the map and the GM writes it down. It can be cleared by work — burning, cutting, days of labour — never by waiting."
                ]
            ],
            "classDC": [
                {
                    "term": "class dc",
                    "rank": 1
